% ch-05-ex-07-mode-error-failing.glp
%
% ⚠ THIS FILE IS MEANT TO FAIL TO LOAD ⚠
%
% This file presents the §5.7.2 mode-error illustration from book pp 51–52,
% byte-exact from the PDF. Loading it should PRODUCE A MODE-ERROR — that
% rejection is the point. Both arguments of `bar(X?, Y).` have inverted
% reader/writer roles versus the procedure declaration, and the type-checker
% says so.
%
% Programs included (byte-exact):
%   §5.7.2 (book pp 51–52): procedure bar(Number?, Number).
%   §5.7.2 (book pp 51–52): bar(X?, Y).                       — the trigger
%
% See ch-05-ex-07-mode-error-corrected.glp for the book-cited corrected form.

%% Declaration: arg 1 consume (`Number?`), arg 2 produce (`Number`).
procedure bar(Number?, Number).

%% Fact `bar(X?, Y).` — X? is a reader at arg 1 (consume position expects a
%% writer); Y is a writer at arg 2 (produce position expects a reader hole).
%% Both modes are inverted. The type-checker rejects the load.
bar(X?, Y).
